-- Source text: Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), Act No. 23 of 2005, as enacted, from the unofficial plain-text rendering No.-23-of-2005.txt.
-- (c) Government of Ireland. Oireachtas Copyright Material is reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS.
-- Part 5 of the Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), "Powers and Duties", in so far as it states a rule with conditions:
--   s 22(3)  a power to make a statutory instrument includes a power to repeal or amend it and (where required) to replace it;
--   s 25     service by post: how it may be effected, and the time at which it is deemed to have been effected.
-- Ss 22(1), 22(2), 23 and 24 state continuing or substitutive rules with no condition that varies; they are recorded as inert in NOTES.md.
--
-- THE TIME OF DELIVERY IS AN INPUT.
-- Section 25 deems service to have been effected "at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post".
-- The Act says nothing about how long the post takes, so that time is supplied by the caller as a DATETIME and never computed.
-- The Act also names no time zone for that time (s 18(i) sends a time by reference to an hour to the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971, which is not in the text),
-- so the function that turns it into a date says in its name that it reads the date in UTC.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`

§ `Named refusals`

-- src:194 | Service by post. 25.—Where an enactment authorises or requires a document to be served by post, by using the word “serve”, “give”, “deliver”, “send” or any other word or expression, the service of the document may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying (where required) and posting a letter containing the document, and in that case the service of the document is deemed, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 25 (src:194)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 25 deems a time of service only where the letter was posted as the section describes` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 25 deems a time of service only where the letter was posted as the section describes"

-- src:194 | Service by post. 25.—Where an enactment authorises or requires a document to be served by post, by using the word “serve”, “give”, “deliver”, “send” or any other word or expression, the service of the document may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying (where required) and posting a letter containing the document, and in that case the service of the document is deemed, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 25 (src:194)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 25 deems the time of service only unless the contrary is proved, and does not say what time of service applies once it is` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 25 deems the time of service only unless the contrary is proved, and does not say what time of service applies once it is"

-- src:190 | (3) A power conferred by an enactment to make a statutory instrument shall be read as including a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions (if any), to repeal or amend a statutory instrument made under that power and (where required) to make another statutory instrument in place of the one so repealed.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 22(3) (src:190)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 22(3) names only the inclusions it lists, so whether the power includes another act is not answered` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 22(3) names only the inclusions it lists, so whether the power includes another act is not answered"

§ `Section 22(3): a power to make a statutory instrument`

DECLARE `An act under a power to make a statutory instrument` IS ONE OF
    `to make the statutory instrument`
    `to repeal a statutory instrument made under the power`
    `to amend a statutory instrument made under the power`
    `to make another statutory instrument in place of one so repealed`
    `to do something else`

-- src:190 | (3) A power conferred by an enactment to make a statutory instrument shall be read as including a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions (if any), to repeal or amend a statutory instrument made under that power and (where required) to make another statutory instrument in place of the one so repealed.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 22(3) (src:190)
GIVEN act IS A `An act under a power to make a statutory instrument`
      `making another in place is required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a power to make a statutory instrument is read as including the power` act `, where` `making another in place is required` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `to make the statutory instrument`                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to repeal a statutory instrument made under the power`          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to amend a statutory instrument made under the power`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to make another statutory instrument in place of one so repealed` THEN `making another in place is required`
    WHEN `to do something else`                                           THEN `section 22(3) names only the inclusions it lists, so whether the power includes another act is not answered`

§ `Section 25: service by post`

DECLARE `A document sent by post` HAS
    `an enactment authorises or requires the document to be served by post, by the word serve, give, deliver, send or any other word` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the letter was properly addressed`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `prepayment is required`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the letter was prepaid`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a letter containing the document was posted`                             IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:194 | Service by post. 25.—Where an enactment authorises or requires a document to be served by post, by using the word “serve”, “give”, “deliver”, “send” or any other word or expression, the service of the document may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying (where required) and posting a letter containing the document, and in that case the service of the document is deemed, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 25 (src:194)
GIVEN p IS A `A document sent by post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`service by post may be effected under section 25` p MEANS
        p's `an enactment authorises or requires the document to be served by post, by the word serve, give, deliver, send or any other word`
    AND p's `the letter was properly addressed`
    AND ((NOT p's `prepayment is required`) OR p's `the letter was prepaid`)
    AND p's `a letter containing the document was posted`

-- src:194 | Service by post. 25.—Where an enactment authorises or requires a document to be served by post, by using the word “serve”, “give”, “deliver”, “send” or any other word or expression, the service of the document may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying (where required) and posting a letter containing the document, and in that case the service of the document is deemed, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 25 (src:194)
GIVEN p IS A `A document sent by post`
      `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATETIME
      `the contrary is proved`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATETIME
`the time at which service is deemed to have been effected` p `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` `the contrary is proved` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `service by post may be effected under section 25` p THEN `section 25 deems a time of service only where the letter was posted as the section describes`
           IF `the contrary is proved` THEN `section 25 deems the time of service only unless the contrary is proved, and does not say what time of service applies once it is`
           OTHERWISE `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`

-- src:178 | (i) Time. Where time is expressed by reference to a specified hour or to a time before or after a specified hour, that time shall be determined by reference to the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 ;
-- src:194 | Service by post. 25.—Where an enactment authorises or requires a document to be served by post, by using the word “serve”, “give”, “deliver”, “send” or any other word or expression, the service of the document may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying (where required) and posting a letter containing the document, and in that case the service of the document is deemed, unless the contrary is proved, to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 25 (src:194); s 18(i) (src:178) names no time zone
GIVEN p IS A `A document sent by post`
      `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATETIME
      `the contrary is proved`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the date in UTC on which service is deemed to have been effected` p `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` `the contrary is proved` MEANS
    Date (`the time at which service is deemed to have been effected` p `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` `the contrary is proved`)
